## 2. DuckDB Medallion Architecture (Step 1)

`src/accesslens/step1_data_layer.py` builds a three-layer DuckDB analytical warehouse (`warehouse/accesslens.duckdb`):

### 2.1 Bronze Layer (`bronze.*`)
* Ingests all **`{{raw_hea_files}}`** HEA CSVs and the Pobal 2022 CSV without row deletion, attaching source filename and SHA-256 digest metadata to every record (`bronze.hea_tab1_multi_year`, `bronze.hea_inst_cross_year` with **`{{bronze_cross_cells}}`** raw cross-tabulation cells, `bronze.hea_county_inst_year`, and `bronze.pobal_ed_2022` with **`{{pobal_ed_count}}`** EDs).

### 2.2 Silver Layer (`silver.*`) & Formal Data Quality Quarantine Rules
Six automated data-quality rules (`outputs/kpis/dq_rule_results.csv`) govern the transition from Bronze to Silver:

| Rule ID | Layer | Scope Checked | Flagged / Quarantined | Engineering Action |
| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |
| **DQ01_SUBTOTAL_SEPARATION** | Bronze -> Silver | `{{bronze_cross_cells}}` cells | `{{silver_quarantined_summary_cells}}` subtotal/total cells | Quarantined to `silver.quarantine_summary_rows`; **`{{silver_clean_cross_cells}}`** atomic cells retained in `silver.hea_inst_cross_clean`. |
| **DQ02_COUNTY_UNMAPPED_QUARANTINE** | Bronze -> Silver | County-year rows | `{{silver_quarantined_county_cells}}` cells (`{{silver_quarantined_county_students_all_years}}` students over `{{n_academic_years}}` yrs; `{{silver_quarantined_county_students_2025_26}}` in `2025/2026`) | Quarantined `N/A` and `Unknown Ireland` domicile rows to `silver.quarantine_unmapped_county`. |
| **DQ03_CROSS_TAB_ADDITIVITY_RECONCILIATION** | Silver | Institution-year-dimension tables | `{{dq_reconciled_tables}}` within `10`; max diff `{{dq_max_rounding_diff}}` | Verified sum of atomic cells against published `Row_Total` within HEA nearest-`{{hea_rounding_base}}` rounding tolerance. |
| **DQ04_NCI_SCOPE_TRANSITION_FLAG** | Silver -> Gold | `{{gold_inst_year_rows}}` institution-years | `{{dq_nci_pre_scope_years}}` pre-scope zero years | Flagged National College of Ireland (`2019/2020` to `2022/2023`) with `in_hea_scope = FALSE` prior to entering SRS scope in `2023/2024`. |
| **DQ05_POBAL_ED_COUNTY_COMPLETENESS** | Bronze -> Silver | `{{pobal_ed_count}}` EDs | `0` unmapped EDs | Deterministic `{{n_cso_ed_prefixes}}`-prefix CSO `ED_ID_STR` mapping to `{{n_counties}}` counties (`silver.county_mapping`). |
| **DQ06_SMALL_CELL_SUPPRESSION** | Silver -> Gold | Atomic cross-tab + county flow cells | `{{suppressed_total_cells}}` small cells (`{{suppressed_inst_dim_cells}}` inst-dim + `{{suppressed_county_inst_cells}}` county-inst) | Flagged `0 < count < {{small_cell_threshold}}` (`count == {{hea_rounding_base}}`) with `suppressed_lt10 = TRUE` and `display_enrolments = '<10'`. |

### 2.3 Deterministic County Mapping (`outputs/kpis/county_mapping.csv`)
The Pobal 2022 Electoral Division file identifies each ED by a 6-character CSO code (`ED_ID_STR`, zero-padded to 6 digits) where the first two digits denote the CSO administrative county (`01` Carlow through `26` Roscommon, plus `47` for Donegal alongside `25`). Mapping on the two-digit CSO prefix rather than text parsing of `COUNTYNAME` avoids substring collisions (for example, `Dublin` vs `South Dublin` or `Cork City` vs `Cork County`) and maps all **`{{pobal_ed_count}}`** EDs (`{{pobal_total_pop_2022}}` population) across the **`{{n_counties}}`** Republic of Ireland counties with zero unmapped records.

### 2.4 Gold Layer (`gold.*`)
* `gold.fact_institution_year` (**`{{gold_inst_year_rows}}`** rows = `{{n_hea_institutions}}` institutions x `{{n_academic_years}}` academic years)
* `gold.fact_institution_dimension_year` (**`{{gold_inst_dim_rows}}`** atomic rows across Programme Type, Age Group, Mode of Study, Field of Study, and Course Level)
* `gold.fact_county_deprivation` (**`{{n_counties}}`** counties with population-weighted Pobal 2022 indices)
* `gold.fact_county_institution_year` (**`{{gold_county_inst_rows}}`** county-to-institution flow records across `{{n_academic_years}}` years)

