## 4. Population-Weighted County Deprivation & Ecological Correlation (Step 3)

For each county $c \in \{1, \dots, {{n_counties}}\}$ containing Electoral Divisions $e \in E_c$ with Census 2022 population $P_e$ (`TOTPOP22`) and Pobal HP 2022 relative deprivation score $D_e$ (`Index22_ED_std_rel_wt`), the population-weighted county score is computed as:

$$\bar{D}_c = \frac{\sum_{e \in E_c} P_e \, D_e}{\sum_{e \in E_c} P_e}$$

And the countyHigher Education Participation Rate per `1,000` residents in academic year $t$ is:

$$R_{c,t} = \frac{\text{Enrolments}_{c,t}}{\sum_{e \in E_c} P_e} \times 1,000$$

### Statistical Inference (`outputs/geography/deprivation_correlations.csv`)
* **Pearson Linear Correlation ($r$):** Evaluated with exact two-sided $t$-distribution $p$-value and Fisher $z$-transformation 95% confidence interval:
  $$z = \text{arctanh}(r), \quad \text{SE}(z) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{n - 3}}, \quad \text{CI}_{95\%} = \tanh\!\left(z \pm 1.96 \, \text{SE}(z)\right)$$
* **Spearman Rank Correlation ($\rho$):** Evaluated with two-sided $p$-value and non-parametric percentile bootstrap 95% confidence interval (`10,000` resamples, fixed seed `42`).
* **Audited Results (`2025/2026`, $n = {{n_counties}}$ counties):**
  * **Pobal Relative Score (`Index22_ED_std_rel_wt`) vs Enrolments per `1,000`:** Pearson $r = {{corr_rel_2025_26_r}}$ (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2025_26_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2025_26_p}}$), Spearman $\rho = {{corr_rel_2025_26_rho}}$ (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_p}}$), OLS slope **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_slope}}`** enrolments per `1,000` per index point ($R^2 = {{corr_rel_2025_26_r2}}$).
  * **Census Match Year (`2022/2023`, $n = {{n_counties}}$ counties):** Pearson $r = {{corr_rel_2022_23_r}}$ (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2022_23_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2022_23_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2022_23_p}}$).
  * **Pooled County Groups (`2025/2026`):** The **`{{n_affluent_counties}}`** net-affluent counties (`Pobal score >= 0`) record a pooled rate of **`{{pooled_affluent_counties_rate_1k_2025_26}}`** per `1,000`, compared with **`{{pooled_deprived_counties_rate_1k_2025_26}}`** per `1,000` across the **`{{n_deprived_counties}}`** below-average counties (`Pobal score < 0`).

