## 5. National Access Plan 2022-2028 KPI & RAG Framework (Step 4)

The National Access Plan 2022-2028 sets headline national targets including:
* Raising the higher education transition rate from disadvantaged areas from **`{{nap_disadv_transition_base}}`** to **`{{nap_disadv_transition_target}}`**.
* Raising mature disadvantaged new entrants from **`{{nap_mature_disadv_base}}`** to **`{{nap_mature_disadv_target}}`**.
* Raising new entrants with a disability from **`{{nap_disability_base}}`** to **`{{nap_disability_target}}`**.
* Raising Traveller new entrants from **`{{nap_traveller_base}}`** to **`{{nap_traveller_target}}`**.

Source: HEA, National Access Plan launch announcement (https://hea.ie/2022/08/31/minister-harris-launches-the-new-national-access-plan-to-drive-equality-of-access-to-higher-education/). The Education and Social Sciences field share is reported as a context indicator only and is not RAG-scored.

Because public SRS aggregate tables do not expose student-level Eircode deprivation or disability status, `src/accesslens/step4_kpi_framework.py` maps **`{{kpi_dictionary_count}}`** public SRS indicators to NAP priority goals with explicit `GREEN`, `AMBER`, and `RED` thresholds (`outputs/kpis/kpi_dictionary.csv` and `outputs/kpis/nap_rag_monitoring.csv`).
